/-- One-step Bochner split for the post-telescope expectation term.

Aligns with Lan Theorem 8.2 proof step 2 after Eq. (8.1.69): the integrated
one-step expression separates into the expected Bregman drop and the raw SFO
noise expectation. Candidate audit: searched SOptLib/Mathlib for finite
integral splitting; `integrable_finset_sum_const_mul` and
`integral_finset_sum_const_mul_eq_zero` cover finite stochastic sums, but not
this scalar Bregman-drop plus raw-observable algebra. This helper is the
route-local Mathlib linearity bridge using `integral_sub`, `integral_add`, and
`integral_const_mul`. -/
private theorem post_telescope_one_step_integral_split
    [MeasurableSpace Ω] {μ : Measure Ω}
    (γ β Γ P : ℝ) (Vprev Vcur raw : Ω → ℝ)
    (hVprev : Integrable Vprev μ) (hVcur : Integrable Vcur μ)
    (hraw : Integrable raw μ)
    (hΓ_ne : Γ ≠ 0) (hOneSub_ne : 1 - P ≠ 0) :
    (∫ ω, γ *
        (β * (1 - P)⁻¹ * (Vprev ω - Vcur ω) +
          P * (1 - P)⁻¹ * raw ω) ∂μ) / Γ =
      γ * β / (Γ * (1 - P)) *
          ((∫ ω, Vprev ω ∂μ) - ∫ ω, Vcur ω ∂μ) +
        γ * P / (Γ * (1 - P)) * (∫ ω, raw ω ∂μ) := by
  have hdiff : Integrable (fun ω => Vprev ω - Vcur ω) μ := hVprev.sub hVcur
  have hleft :
      Integrable
        (fun ω => β * (1 - P)⁻¹ * (Vprev ω - Vcur ω)) μ :=
    hdiff.const_mul (β * (1 - P)⁻¹)
  have hright :
      Integrable
        (fun ω => P * (1 - P)⁻¹ * raw ω) μ :=
    hraw.const_mul (P * (1 - P)⁻¹)
  rw [integral_const_mul]
  rw [integral_add hleft hright]
  rw [integral_const_mul]
  rw [integral_sub hVprev hVcur]
  rw [integral_const_mul]
  field_simp [hΓ_ne, hOneSub_ne]


/-- Common post-telescope split/relax bridge for Theorem 8.2 expected bounds.

Aligns with Lan Theorem 8.2 proof step 2 after Eq. (8.1.69): the integrated
finite telescope splits into an expected Bregman-drop window and a raw SFO-noise
window, then `(M+||δ||_*)^2` is relaxed to `M^2+||δ||_*^2`. Candidate audit:
considered SOptLib `outputWindow_sum_sub_succ`, `expectedOutput_eq_weighted_sum_div`,
